From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: Strikers 101 has a FREE PLAY button into training
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

Training (tweak patch 0038) could start only from the launcher. Strikers
101's list of lessons now has a FREE PLAY button at the bottom right,
beside its BACK: the navigation's PLAY button (the Cup's PLAY NOW, the
stadium select's), whose text is the host's
(mscharged_tweak_training_free_play_text, English without it). No layout
changes: the button, its slides and its place are the navigation's own,
and its pointer region is the one the stadium select gives it
(SetPlayButtonBounds). The scene puts the navigation's PLAY NOW text back
as it goes.

Pressed, the list plays its out slide and the game goes on as the main
menu's Domination does (GM_FRIENDLY, no teams, no sides), marked as
training's match (g_bTrainingMatch, after SetMode, which clears it), into
Domination's own screens from its captains on: captains, sidekicks, sides
and stadium, then the match. Domination's gameplay options are left out:
training plays its own match (one to 10 goals, without cheats). The
captains share the lessons' camera (fe_presentation's
TransitionMainMenuToTutorial and TransitionMainMenuToGrudgeMatch both go to
fechoosecaptains), so they come straight after the list. The list's scroll
position is kept in the challenge data for the way back.

The way back is the lessons' list too:
- the captains' BACK, which would go to Domination's gameplay options, goes
  back to the list, with the scroll position it had, and the game in the
  mode the main menu's Strikers 101 gives it (GM_CHALLENGE: SetMode clears
  the training mark);
- a training match never ends on its goals and is left from the pause
  menu; one from FREE PLAY goes back to the list, as a lesson does (the
  challenge branch of the front end's return, with its
  TransitionGameToStrikerChallenge). g_bFreePlayMatch says where the match
  came from: the list sets it with g_bTrainingMatch, and SetMode clears
  both. The launcher's Start training still ends in the main menu, and so
  does a replay of a FREE PLAY match.

Between the two scores, where the HUD says FIRST TO 10 (HUD_FIRST_TO), a
training match says FREE PLAY: the host's text for the button, or FREE PLAY
when the host gives none.

